  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the capacities of federal, state and local governments in Mexico to respond to internal displacement with a gender focus &#x2013; phase IIStrengthening the capacities of federal, state and local governments in Mexico to respond to internal displacement with a gender focus &#x2013; phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x200b;&#x200b;In Mexico, internal displacement is an ongoing issue due to a number of diverse and multi-factors drivers including environmental challenges, economic shifts, infrastructure development and security concerns. This project aims to contribute to improved multisectoral, coordinated and targeted protection responses and prevention mechanisms for internally displaced persons and communities at risk of displacement in Mexico. &#x200b;To achieve this, an updated gender-sensitive comparative case study on inter-institutional coordination mechanisms on differential IDP and host community protection will be made available to policymakers (Output 1.1); an inclusive guide for the recovery and re-establishment of identity documents, as well as registration processes, will be made available to support the development of regulatory recommendations in Chiapas (Output 1.2); and authorities in Tijuana will have access to technical support to operationalize the evidence-based recommendations developed during phase 1 (Output 1.3). Finally, local authorities and human rights organizations in Oaxaca will have access to an assessment, action plan, guide and gender-sensitive training in conflict prevention and management to address the root causes of internal displacement (Output 2.1). By achieving these outputs, it is expected that federal, state and local stakeholders in Mexico effectively utilize up-to-date research and implement evidence-based recommendations, incorporating intersectional gender analysis to protect IDPs and communities at risk (Outcome 1); and that the state authorities in Oaxaca effectively utilize gender-sensitive, inclusive and protection-centered community stabilization and alternative conflict resolution tools to prevent internal displacement and ensure IDPs protection (Outcome 2). &#x200b;</narrative>
  </description>
